# Ordin Desktop
error-dsk-agent-profile-only = That action isn't available in ordin on your desktop.
error-dsk-dashboard-not-found = That dashboard can't be found. It may have been removed.
error-dsk-dashboard-no-report = This dashboard has no report to save yet. Refresh it, then try again.
error-dsk-data-root-unwritable = ordin can't save its files on this computer. Check there is free space and that you can write to your user folder.
error-dsk-dialog-cancelled = Saving was cancelled.
error-dsk-draft-list-failed = ordin couldn't check your drafts just now. It will try again.
error-dsk-link-refused = ordin can't open that link.
error-dsk-link-register-failed = ordin couldn't set itself up to open its links. Links to ordin may not work.
error-dsk-logs-clear-failed = ordin couldn't clear all of its logs. Close anything that has a log file open, then try again.
error-dsk-log-file-not-deleted = ordin couldn't delete an old log file. It will try again later.
error-dsk-models-blocked = Your network stopped the memory download. Try again later, or on another network.
error-dsk-models-disk-full = There isn't enough free space on this computer to get memory ready. Free up about 350 MB, then try again.
error-dsk-models-interrupted = The memory download stopped before it finished. Try again; it carries on from where it stopped.
error-dsk-models-mismatch = The memory download arrived damaged, so ordin didn't use it. Try again; if it happens again, choose Save logs for support… in Settings › Diagnostics.
error-dsk-models-not-in-build = This version of ordin can't get memory ready. Install the latest version of ordin.
error-dsk-models-offline = ordin couldn't connect to get memory ready. Check you're online, then try again.
error-dsk-models-write-failed = ordin couldn't save what memory needs on this computer. Try again; if it happens again, choose Save logs for support… in Settings › Diagnostics.
error-dsk-notify-failed = ordin couldn't show a notification. Check notifications are allowed for ordin on your computer.
error-dsk-picker-unavailable = The folder chooser wouldn't open. Try again.
error-dsk-preferences-unreadable = ordin couldn't read your preferences, so it is using the usual ones.
error-dsk-preferences-write-failed = Your preference wasn't saved. Try again.
error-dsk-preference-value-invalid = That value isn't allowed for this preference. Choose another.
error-dsk-presentation-unreadable = ordin can't add slides to that file. Choose a PowerPoint presentation (.pptx) that isn't protected with a password.
error-dsk-relay-timeout = The sign-in wasn't finished in your browser in time. Try again.
error-dsk-relay-url-refused = ordin didn't trust that sign-in address, so it stopped. Start the sign-in again from ordin.
error-dsk-save-copy-failed = ordin couldn't save the file where you chose. Choose another place and try again.
error-dsk-shutdown-step-timeout = Part of ordin took too long to close. It closed anyway.
error-dsk-sidecar-missing = A program ordin needs is missing from its install. Reinstall ordin.
error-dsk-ssh-keygen-missing = This computer has no tool for making SSH keys. Choose a key you already have instead.
error-dsk-ssh-key-not-made = ordin couldn't make a new SSH key. Try again.
error-dsk-ssh-key-unknown = That key isn't in your SSH folder any more. Choose another one.
error-dsk-ssh-no-key = Choose an SSH key first.
error-dsk-move-copy-failed = ordin couldn't copy itself to your Applications folder. Check there is space on the disk and try again.
error-dsk-move-not-needed = ordin is already in an Applications folder.
error-dsk-move-start-failed = ordin is now in your Applications folder but couldn't start from there. Quit ordin and open it from your Applications folder.
error-dsk-start-failed = ordin couldn't start. Close any other ordin window, then try again; if it keeps happening, reinstall ordin.
error-dsk-support-log-unreadable = ordin couldn't read one of its log files, so the support file was saved without it.
error-dsk-update-check-failed = ordin couldn't check for updates. Try again later.
error-dsk-update-install-failed = The update couldn't be downloaded or checked. Try again.
error-dsk-writes-not-attributed = ordin couldn't start because it can't record who made changes. Reinstall ordin.
